# NOTE: api/bundle.js and sallog/api/bundle.js MUST stay in version control.
# They look like disposable build artifacts, but vercel.json routes /api/(.*)
# to /api/bundle.js and Vercel only registers it as a serverless function when
# the file is already present in the repository — the buildCommand regenerating
# it is not enough. Untracking them took every /api/* route to 404 in
# production (2026-08-09). Do not add them here.
*.local
drizzle

.vercel
CREDENCIAIS.txt
# Added by code-review-graph
.code-review-graph/

# Agent scratch space — these are separate git repositories. Committing one
# lands a gitlink (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules entry, and then every
# checkout logs `fatal: No url found for submodule path` while the directory
# clones empty. Two of them reached main before this rule existed; a third came
# in via .claude/skills/get-shit-done, which was a clone rather than plain
# files. If you add a skill, commit its files — never a nested repo.
.claude/worktrees/
